{#- The canary (H5.2b, docs/target-architecture/host/h5-pi-compose.md). It is the first service the
    Pi's `homelab` project runs and moves nothing: no Ansible role ever deployed it. It proves
    three things before any real service moves (H5.6 to H5.9):
      1. compose-run brings a one-service project up through homelab-compose.service;
      2. a plain inventory variable renders into the compose file at package build time
         (HOMELAB_DOMAIN below). `domain` is not a SOPS key since #5087, so it never goes
         through compose.env. The canary reads no secret and has no `env_file:` (operator ruling
         2026-10-24, h5-pi-compose.md *Open questions* 7), so the proof that an included file
         receives a value from compose.env waits for the first move that carries a real secret;
      3. removing a service removes its container (`up --remove-orphans`, H5.10).
    `sleep infinity` costs about 1 MB. There is no healthcheck: a probe forks runc every interval
    on a 512 MB board, and "the container runs" is the whole claim, which `--wait` waits for and
    the recovery heartbeat watches by name. H5.4 bumps the digest to measure an unattended pull,
    and H5.10 removes this file. -#}
services:
  pi-canary:
    container_name: pi-canary
    image: busybox:stable@sha256:73aaf090f3d85aa34ee199857f03fa3a95c8ede2ffd4cc2cdb5b94e566b11662
    command: ["sleep", "infinity"]
    restart: unless-stopped
    read_only: true
    cap_drop:
      - ALL
    security_opt:
      - no-new-privileges:true
    environment:
      - HOMELAB_DOMAIN={{ domain }}
    deploy:
      resources:
        limits:
          cpus: '0.05'
          memory: 8M
        reservations:
          cpus: '0.01'
          memory: 2M
